y on trade, collective security, petroleum cooperation and the Olympic movement.","format":"single_best_answer","references":[{"file":"WHO — About WHO","verificationUrl":"https://www.who.int/about","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B02-E03","title":"WHO — About WHO","url":"https://www.who.int/about","support_summary":"WHO directs and coordinates international public-health work.","verification_status":"supporting_web_text_read","checked_on":"2026-10-07","verification_method":"Author read the cited supporting web text; not independent expert certification.","source_type":"institutional","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"previous_batch_inherited"}}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":161,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":1,"topic74":"WHO international health role","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B02:who-international-health-role","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:who-international-health-role"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"supporting_text_records_available","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"f956f9f46e3b049fa614e00ef3d7c9a1056b82b5d6e8dbbdc906e98c96d4d0e3","fingerprint":"caa366b9c68d31ce5aab","review100":{"date":"2026-10-09","scope":"Stem, five alternatives, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"supporting_text_records_available","decision":"adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B02-20261007-162","qid":950162,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-162","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-162"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"History & Politics","group":"ILO tripartite representation","stem":"Which three groups are represented in the ILO’s tripartite structure?","choices":["Governments, employers and workers","Workers, shareholders and central bankers","National governments, regional governments and municipalities","Governments, judges and journalists","Governments, employers and consumers"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":"Governments, employers and workers","explanation":"Including workers and employers alongside governments makes labour standards a subject of organized social dialogue. “Tripartite” refers to these three participant groups.","format":"single_best_answer","references":[{"file":"ILO — About the ILO","verificationUrl":"https://www.ilo.org/about-ilo","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B02-E04","title":"ILO — About the ILO","url":"https://www.ilo.org/about-ilo","support_summary":"The ILO brings together governments, employers and workers in its tripartite structure.","verification_status":"supporting_web_text_read","checked_on":"2026-10-07","verification_method":"Author read the cited supporting web text; not independent expert certification.","source_type":"institutional","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"previous_batch_inherited"}},{"file":"V100 institutional reference check","verificationUrl":"https://www.ilo.org/resource/article/tripartism-action-strengthening-workers-rights-through-collaboration","checkedAt":"2026-10-09","supportScope":"Governments, employers and workers"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":162,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":1,"topic74":"ILO tripartite representation","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B02:ilo-tripartite-representation","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:ilo-tripartite-representation"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"supporting_text_records_available","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"a60d9a4cbcd12fa1cbce2e112d70ed73b9c6b6dc3a8b2e631f7a340adbaf3d13","fingerprint":"29d6e68d1238acb428d8","review100":{"date":"2026-10-09","scope":"Stem, five alternatives, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"supporting_text_records_available","decision":"adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B02-20261007-163","qid":950163,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-163","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B02-20261007-163"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"History & Politics","group":"UN Security Council veto and abstention","stem":"Which action by a permanent Security Council member can block a substantive draft resolution?","choices":["Voting in favour","Casting a negative vote","Abstaining from the vote","Requesting that a speech be translated","Changing its representative between meetings"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":"Casting a negative vote","explanation":"The veto concerns a permanent member’s negative vote on a non-procedural matter. An abstention is not the same thing as exercising a veto.","format":"distinction","references":[{"file":"UN Security Council — Voting System","verificationUrl":"https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/voting-system","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B02-E05","title":"UN Security Council — Voting System","url":"https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/voting-system","support_summary":"A negative vote by a permanent member can block a substantive draft resolution; abstention is not itself a veto.","verification_status":"supporting_web_text_read","checked_on":"2026-10-07","verification_method":"Author read the cited supporting web text; not independent expert certification.","source_type":"institutional","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"previous_batch_inherited"}},{"file":"V100 institutional reference check","verificationUrl":"https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/voting-system","checkedAt":"2026-10-09","supportScope":"Negative permanent-member vote and abstention distinction"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"read