 the famous streets in forced perspective behind the stage facade.","format":"matching","references":[{"file":"Encyclopaedia reference — Teatro Olimpico","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teatro_Olimpico","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B03-S-Teatro_Olimpico","key":"Teatro_Olimpico","title":"Encyclopaedia reference — Teatro Olimpico","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teatro_Olimpico","source_type":"tertiary_encyclopaedia","verification_status":"reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","checked_at":null,"support_scope":"Reference supplied for this topic; no claim that its live text was read in this pass.","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"reference_only"}}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":221,"canonical_number":null,"revision95":1,"topic74":"Teatro Olimpico division of authorship","skill74":"context_relation","testedRelation95":"B03:teatro-olimpico-division-of-authorship","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["TOPIC:teatro-olimpico-division-of-authorship"],"workIds95":[],"evidenceStatus95":"reference_only_pending_external_check","exactDuplicateOf95":[],"sourceSnapshotHash95":"531e858f93a32df1a74427552862968ccfa2aba319326e3f6a9f2c4c11c121e0","fingerprint":"cb467ddd85aab8ef9797","review100":{"date":"2026-10-09","scope":"Stem, five alternatives, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"reference_only_pending_external_check","decision":"adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B03-20261007-222","qid":950222,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B03-20261007-222","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B03-20261007-222"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"Architecture","group":"Tempietto classical form","stem":"Bramante's Tempietto adapts which ancient architectural idea to a Christian memorial?","choices":["A ci