, correct answer and explanation reviewed. Retained source provenance is not an assertion of fresh external verification.","sourceVerification":"reference_only_pending_external_check","decision":"adopted"}},{"id":"ARCHED-B03-20261007-300","qid":950300,"nodeId":"REVIEW95-ARCHED-B03-20261007-300","relatedNodeIds":["REVIEW95-ARCHED-B03-20261007-300"],"sourceAtlasNodeIds":[],"major":"Art History","group":"Bruegel Peasant Wedding: society and period","stem":"Which social and historical setting best fits the painting shown?","choices":["A revolutionary public meeting — nineteenth-century Paris","An aristocratic court ceremony — seventeenth-century France","An imperial banquet — eighteenth-century Russia","A peasant celebration — sixteenth-century Netherlands","An ancient Greek religious festival — fifth-century BCE Athens"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":"A peasant celebration — sixteenth-century Netherlands","explanation":"Bruegel's Peasant Wedding depicts a rural wedding celebration in the sixteenth-century Netherlandish world. Food, service and social grouping—not a mythological hero or royal portrait—organize the scene.","format":"visual_context","references":[{"file":"Encyclopaedia reference — The Peasant Wedding","verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Peasant_Wedding","sourceMetadata95":{"id":"B03-S-Peasant_Wedding","key":"Peasant_Wedding","title":"Encyclopaedia reference — The Peasant Wedding","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Peasant_Wedding","source_type":"tertiary_encyclopaedia","verification_status":"reference_locator_not_retrieved_this_pass","checked_at":null,"support_scope":"Reference supplied for this topic; no claim that its live text was read in this pass.","quoted_text":false,"verification_record_origin":"reference_only"}}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-review-v100","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"seriesNumber95":300,"canon